Z||000003||beer_stud_21||07-23-2001||02:51 PM||||PIP is short for "Pennocks Image Poster"  I've never seen it run personallly.  But I'm pretty you select the images you want to post in your message and it:  A) Uploads the selected pictures to Cliffs uploads folder.  B) Generates the UBB code for displaying them.  Then you essentually just copy the generated code into your message when you write it.  As for the computer reader, I would have to look into that.  it might actually not be that hard.  What kinds of Macs do you boys have?  I have a G3 upgraded PM 8500, PB  1400, and a Duo 230  I also take care of a iMac DV, and soon a iBook 500 (parents computers).  The fiero computer reader would probably have to be a serial connection so it wouldnt work on some of the newer Powerbooks.  (Lombard and newer-Anything with only USB)<P>tell me what you guys thing.<P>Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000004||kslish||07-23-2001||04:06 PM||||I use PIP via Virtual PC 3.0 Windows emulation software on my Mac.  Works like a charm.  <P>Course, if someone wants to develop a Mac version, that would be cool too.<P>I currently have a 6400 with a G3 processor upgrade, ATI video, 104MB RAM, 60gig HD, CD burner, cable modem and some other stuff.  Nothing too impressive (especially considering I work for Apple part time).  Wish they would start giving me free hardware in addition to all the free software I get in addition to the occasional pay check  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Been throwing around the idea of getting a cheap old G3 upgraded 9500 that I can transfer all my old legacy hardware too (I have a LOT of serial and SCSI stuff) to gain some extra PCI slots and the ability to run OS X (yes the 7500-9500 series can run OS X).  Apple sent me the OS CD-ROM and I have nothing to run it on.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I would like to get a PowerBook also though soon.  May wait until the current iBooks (they are NICE) become available used....or get me an old PB 1400 or something to hold me over for a while.<P>Ken S.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||beer_stud_21||07-23-2001||06:23 PM||||kslish,<P>Cool man.  What do you do for apple.  I used to do their tech support.  I was actually working for a subcontractor (sykes) and they sucked a big one.  I was happy to see apple pull their tech support in house.  I left about 3 weeks before they pulled out of sykes.  Good riddence.  Using VPC for PIP works, but its a bit overkill and a pain to load up VPC just for that.  If you wanna, could you take a couple screenshots of PIP and send them to me?  I dont have vpc installed on any of my machines.  <P>-marlin||||reg||1
Z||000006||Yellow88GT||07-24-2001||08:52 AM||||Hey kslish,<P>I have an 8500 with a G3 card running OS X.<P>Check out this web site: <A HREF="http://eshop.macsales.com/OSXCenter/framework.cfm?page=UnsupportedUtilityX.html" TARGET=_blank>http://eshop.macsales.com/OSXCenter/framework.cfm?page=UnsupportedUtilityX.html</A> <P>I think it will work with the 6000 series as well. <P>Just one problem,<BR>it is a little on the slow side   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Jerry<p>[This message has been edited by Yellow88GT (edited 07-24-2001).]||||reg||1
